{"abstract":"This article explores how the concept of play as a vision of software that establishes new relations with digital technologies. This article argues that play has a fundamental role in shaping human engagement with software, and the cultural phenomena that derive from that engagement.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Sicart, Miguel Angel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384551"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Play","Relational strategies","software society"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"playing software the role of the ludic in the software society","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85564162/Playing_software_the_role_of_the_ludic_in_the_software_society.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384551","identifier":[{"id":"85085359326","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-df4abdd3-307d-4ce8-a213-855c34908aa0"],"keyword":["Play","artificial intelligence","relational strategies","software society"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-085CBE2780F2C04E444247A79FCBDFB5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85564162/Playing_software_the_role_of_the_ludic_in_the_software_society.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Miguel Angel","key":"sicartpau","last":"Sicart","locid":"689427b5-8d2a-44f3-b291-6db6ba598305","name":"Sicart, Miguel Angel","orcid":"0000-0002-8356-5394","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/1369118x.2020.1764078","issn":["1369118X","14684462"],"issn_org":["1369118X"],"journal":"Information, Communication & Society","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Information, Communication & Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085359326"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-df4abdd3-307d-4ce8-a213-855c34908aa0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Playing software: the role of the ludic in the software society","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384551","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"These days, whether the problem is climate change or boredom, there is an app for that. The rhetoric of problem and solution, accelerated by commercial needs and salvific tech gurus, implies that software can save the world. This paper wants to start a movement/rebellion against the ubiquitous equation of P(problem) + S(software) = S(solution) as a rational approach to the ailments of this world. We question the technological effort to \"playfully\" afford order and control to humans through the provision of computational rules. Instead, we propose an alternative approach: designing 'pataphysical software to address familiar but ultimately imaginary problems. Defined by poet Alfred Jarry, 'pataphysics is the science of imaginary problems. Adopting the methods of 'pataphysics, we have developed mobile applications that explore invented problems and provide no solutions for them. We demonstrate how such an approach allows us to ask design questions through an aesthetic 'pataphysical practice of software development.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Sicart, Miguel Angel","Shklovski, Irina"],"cuid":["S02-096.15-038393"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","end":"2020-07-10","place":"Eindhoven, nl","start":"2020-07-06","title":"2020 ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems, DIS 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Art","Data","Design","Mobile apps","Pataphysics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pataphysical software ridiculous technological solutions for imaginary problems","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85564045/PataphysicalSoftware_Accepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-096.15-038393","identifier":[{"id":"85090503221","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-da5c9817-89e6-481d-8f65-af73661821cf","ku-ec98cab7-8ed8-4c05-a27e-81f0b53254d6"],"keyword":["'Pataphysics","art","data","design","mobile apps"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D5A0CB720CE79055E15B767C67DEF1DA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://miguelsicart.net/publications/PataphysicalSoftware_Accepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85564045/PataphysicalSoftware_Accepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centred Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Miguel Angel","key":"sicartpau","last":"Sicart","locid":"689427b5-8d2a-44f3-b291-6db6ba598305","name":"Sicart, Miguel Angel","orcid":"0000-0002-8356-5394","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Irina","key":"shklovskipau","last":"Shklovski","locid":"e5067505-4088-