{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Sicart, Miguel Angel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383548"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"papers please ethics","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383548","ids":["itu-9c3e4fa1-70cf-4bea-9f1e-4880788f68d6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7C397CDD6602593B0351434A89648DAF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Miguel Angel","key":"sicartpau","last":"Sicart","locid":"689427b5-8d2a-44f3-b291-6db6ba598305","name":"Sicart, Miguel Angel","orcid":"0000-0002-8356-5394","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nina","key":"huntemannpedh","last":"Huntemann","name":"Huntemann, Nina","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthew Thomas","key":"paynepedh","last":"Payne","name":"Payne, Matthew Thomas","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781479802142"],"pages":"149-156","publisher":"New York University Press","status":"p","title":"How To Play Videogames"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9c3e4fa1-70cf-4bea-9f1e-4880788f68d6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Papers, Please: Ethics","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383548","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The author proposes a rhetoric of computational play as a perspective for the analysis of the ludic in the Information Age. Combining concepts from the philosophy of information and postphenomenology with different theories of play, he argues that there is a play element shaping the cultural impact of computational media and that this kind of play is experienced as either sub-mission or resistance to the pleasures of computation. Both kind of experiences help develop new forms of understanding and create the cultures of the Information Age.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Sicart, Miguel Angel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381591"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computational Media","Digital Play","Philosophy of information","Postphenomenology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quixotean play in the age of computation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.journalofplay.org/sites/www.journalofplay.org/files/pdf-articles/10-3-Article-1-Quixotean-Play.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381591","ids":["itu-1525f0c3-6f1b-4ce2-9a33-eb852daee264"],"keyword":["computational media","digital play","philosophy of information","postphenomenology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B62F8EE7D0F5D185F91AB0389FBE22F0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83472481/QP_Preprint.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.journalofplay.org/sites/www.journalofplay.org/files/pdf-articles/10-3-Article-1-Quixotean-Play.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Miguel Angel","key":"sicartpau","last":"Sicart","locid":"689427b5-8d2a-44f3-b291-6db6ba598305","name":"Sicart, Miguel Angel","orcid":"0000-0002-8356-5394","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19380399"],"issn_org":["19380402"],"issue":"3","journal":"American Journal of Play","publisher":"The Strong National Museum of Play","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Play","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1525f0c3-6f1b-4ce2-9a33-eb852daee264"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Quixotean Play in the Age of Computation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381591","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Fitness trackers promise a longer and better life for the people who engage with them. What is forgotten in their analysis for HCI, though, is how they re-conceptualise the very notion of what constitutes a 'step'. We discuss everyday edge cases illustrating how fitness trackers fail to address goals and ideals of people using them. They merely re-affirm the fitness of already fit people and can have an adversarial effect on others. For future designers, we offer strategies to become aware of their own biases and provide implications for designers potentially leading to more non-normative and diverse designs of trackers.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Spiel, Katta","Kayali, Fares","Horvath, Louise","Penkler, Michael","Harrer, Sabine","Sicart, Miguel Angel","Hammer, Jessica"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382156"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Austrian Institute for Applied Telecommunications","BTK – Art & Design Berlin","Carnegie Mellon University","Technical University of Munich","Vienna University of Technology"],"keyword":["Design Bias","Fitness Trackers","Human Computer Interaction","Inclusive design","Step Re conceptualization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fitter happier more productive the normative ontology of fitness trackers","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83472571/altchi_Fitness_Preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382156","iden