{"abstract":"This paper is concerned with designing for immediate play, the experience that a player has when joining a game designed for being played without particular preparation. Museum games, urban games, casual sports, and ad-hoc multiplayer video games are kinds of games that facilitate immediate play situations. After a detailed explanation of immediate play, we analyze the context of the immediate play situation, which is mostly characterized by an overlap between different realities of the experience. The article continues by describing various design dimensions and outlining the design space those offer using examples and expert opinions. While most practices and game examples mentioned in this paper are from non-digital games, a special focus is put on the role of technology in immediately playable experiences. Still, the examined design dimensions are independent of the technological foundation of the game. This paper provides a starting point for designing better immediate play situations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pichlmair, Martin","Mech, Lena","Sicart, Miguel Angel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382362"],"event":{"acronym":"FGD(?)","end":"2017-08-17","place":"Hyannis, us","start":"2017-08-14","title":"FDG 2017: Foundations of Digital Games","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Game design","Immediate Play","Museum Games","Pervasive games","Play Design","Urban Games"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing for immediate play","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82271253/designing_play.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382362","identifier":[{"id":"85030767758","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-494eb6b6-f11b-494e-89cb-a2f6df186d9f"],"keyword":["Game Design","Immediate Play","Museum Games","Pervasive Games","Play Design","Urban Games"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-75B6CCFA07B3F29CFCB69474F336C632"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82271253/designing_play.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"pichlmairpau","last":"Pichlmair","locid":"ddcdfda8-c5ea-4e67-b0ea-21ba86966197","name":"Pichlmair, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-8828-9723","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lena","key":"mechpau","last":"Mech","name":"Mech, Lena","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Miguel Angel","key":"sicartpau","last":"Sicart","locid":"689427b5-8d2a-44f3-b291-6db6ba598305","name":"Sicart, Miguel Angel","orcid":"0000-0002-8356-5394","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3102071.3102075","isbn":["9781450353199"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"FDG '17","title":"Proceedings of the 12th International Conference on the Foundations of Digital Games"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030767758"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-494eb6b6-f11b-494e-89cb-a2f6df186d9f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designing for Immediate Play","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382362","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"An Theorien und Diskussionen über die Stadt mangelt es nicht, denn Städte dienen uns u.a. als Projektionsfläche zur Auseinandersetzung mit unserer Vergangenheit, der Gegenwart und unserer Zukunft. Diese Ausgabe 1 (2016) der Navigationen untersucht spielerische Formen dieser Auseinandersetzung in und mit der Stadt durch die sogenannten playful urban arts. The city has been discussed and theorized widely, and it continues to serve as a space in which our sense of the present, past, and future is constantly negotiated. This issue 1 (2016) of Navigationen examines new ways of engaging with cities through what are called the playful urban arts. Playful engagements with the urban environment frequently strive to create new ways of imagining and experiencing the city. In and through play, city spaces can become playgrounds that have the potential to transform people’s sense of themselves as human actors in an urban network of spatially bound and socio-economically grounded actions. Emerging from the playin’siegen urban games festival 2015, the essays and panel discussions assembled in this issue provide an interdisciplinary account of the contemporary playful urban arts. Wiht contributions by Miguel Sicart, Andreas Rauscher, Daniel Stein, Judith Ackermann and Martin Reiche, Michael Straeubig and Sebastian Quack, Marianne Halblaub Miranda and Martin Knöll, and Anne Lena Hartman.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Sicart, Miguel Angel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383909"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["city as playground","playful urban arts","urban gaming"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"play and the city","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dokumentix.ub.uni-siegen.de/opus/volltexte/2016/1004/pdf/Navigationen_Playin_the_city.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383909","identifier":[{"id":"84969764628","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b534c254-793a-4b78-b013-b8a6bd49be5f"],"keyword":["city as playground","playful urban arts","urban gaming"],"lang":"English","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2B837D72EC6F4A1378E8AF066A6BCF9B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dokumentix.ub.uni-siegen.de/opus/volltexte/2016/1004/pdf/Navigationen_Playin_the_city.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Miguel Angel","key":"sicartpau","last":"Sicart","locid":"689427b5-8d2a-44f3-b291-6db6ba598305","name":"Sicart, Miguel Angel","orcid":"0000-0002-8356-5394","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16191641"],"journal":"Navigationen. Zeitschrift für Medien- und Kulturwissenschaften","pages":"25-40","status":"p","title":"Navigationen. Zeitschrift für Medien- und Kulturwissenschaften"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b534c254-793a-4b78-b013-b8a6bd49be5f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Play and the City","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383909","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
